# T0187 — AI confirmation and review UX for Tier 2 and Tier 3

**Task:** T0187 (id 202) — AI: confirmation and review UX for Tier 2 and Tier 3
**State at plan:** `ready` · Priority: medium · Project: TaskMesh (4)
**Parent:** T0192 Guardrails and governance (group); design decisions in epic T0177
**Depends on:** T0185 (complete). T0186 (Undo) is already on `main` and stays as-is for Tier 1.
**Branch (after approval):** `T0187-review-ux`
**Version on finish-up:** PATCH (no new `drizzle/*.sql`; proposals stay client-side)

## Size / dependencies

One review surface plus a shared confirm card. Depends-on T0185 is complete. Required-by tasks stay out of this pass: T0200 duplicate detection, T0215 quick-capture UI, T0235 MCP multi-round-trip confirmations. No split and no new deferred Task.

## What exists

- Chat proposals render as one-click Apply / Dismiss cards in `AssistantPanel`. The client ignores `planTier`.
- The server classifies a turn as one change plan (max tier, blast-radius escalation) and stamps `tier` on each proposal SSE event. Tier 1 plans auto-apply (T0186). Tier 2 and Tier 3 both become the same cards.
- Apply is `POST /api/v1/assistant/proposals/apply`. Deletes are denied. Nothing checks whether the target changed after the proposal was made.
- Mesh suggestions are a separate one-click “Accept link” / “Dismiss” on the canvas card. They post `/api/v1/links`, not assistant proposals.

## Decisions

| # | Topic | Decision |
|---|--------|----------|
| 1 | Which tier drives the UI | The **plan** tier. Tier 1 keeps auto-apply. Tier 2 keeps one-click cards. Tier 3 opens one review dialog for every operation in that turn. A mixed turn does not show both |
| 2 | Tier 2 card | Shared `AiProposalCard`: heading, summary, field diff, Apply, Dismiss. Assistant uses it for Tier 2. Mesh suggestion rows use the same card in a compact variant (confidence bar stays in the mesh shell; Apply / Dismiss replace Accept link / Dismiss). Mesh still posts `/api/v1/links` |
| 3 | Tier 3 dialog | Modal `role="dialog"` with a focus trap. Operations grouped by project (creates with no project under “No project”). Each row: checkbox, summary, diff. Checkboxes start **unchecked**. **Approve selected** applies only checked rows and leaves the rest in the dialog. **Reject all** dismisses every remaining row. Escape and the backdrop close the dialog without applying; a “Review changes” control reopens it |
| 4 | Diff | Updates include a server `before` snapshot of the proposed keys. The row shows `before → after`. Creates show proposed fields as additions. Deletes, if one ever appears, render disabled with “A person deletes this in the app” and are omitted from Approve selected |
| 5 | Expiry | Update proposals carry `baseUpdatedAt` from the target row at proposal time. Apply returns **409** when the row’s `updatedAt` differs or the row is gone. The card and the review row show **Expired**, the checkbox is disabled, and Apply is refused. Creates do not expire this way. No proposals table |
| 6 | Client plan stamp | `streamAssistantChat` returns `planTier` and `planEscalations` from the `done` event. The panel stores them with that turn’s proposals |
| 7 | Keyboard | Real buttons and checkboxes, visible focus, dialog labelled, no mouse-only control. `npm run lint` stays at zero warnings |
| 8 | Out of scope | Persisting proposals across reload, admin tier editor (T0189), user matrix (T0190), MCP confirmations (T0235), changing Tier 1 auto-apply / Undo |

## Work items

### 1. Proposal snapshot

When the assistant emits an update proposal, load the target’s `updatedAt` and the current values of the keys in `fields`. Attach `before` and `baseUpdatedAt` on the SSE `proposal` payload. Creates omit both.

### 2. Apply guard

In the apply route, after the existing policy check: if `baseUpdatedAt` is present, compare it to the live row. Mismatch or missing row → 409 and no write. Ignore a client-supplied tier. Deletes stay 403.

### 3. Shared card

`client/src/components/shared/AiProposalCard.tsx` (compact and full). Assistant Tier 2 list uses it. Mesh suggestion items use the compact variant for the action row and summary; the link request stays on the existing mutation.

### 4. Review dialog

`client/src/components/shared/AiReviewDialog.tsx`. Open when a turn’s `planTier` is 3 and proposals remain. Group by project. Approve selected calls the existing apply endpoint per checked row, skips expired and delete rows, and reports a per-row error without clearing the others. Reject all uses the existing dismiss feedback when `auditId` is set.

### 5. Tests

- Apply helper: matching `baseUpdatedAt` proceeds to the current write path; a newer `updatedAt` returns the 409 predicate; a missing row does too. No new Postgres suite if the predicate can be unit-tested the way the delete deny is.
- Client: a small pure helper groups proposals by project and marks a row expired when `baseUpdatedAt` is set and a check function says the target moved (the UI receives expiry from a failed apply or from a `stale: true` flag if we add a lightweight recheck — prefer marking stale only after a 409, plus disabling Apply when the user already saw 409).

## QA checklist (after implementation)

1. A Tier 2 chat proposal (single create or update) still shows a card. Apply writes the record. Dismiss removes the card.
2. A Tier 3 turn (delete-shaped, cross-project, other user’s record, or a plan over the blast-radius thresholds) opens the review dialog. Nothing is written until a checkbox is checked and Approve selected is used.
3. Unchecked rows stay after Approve selected. Reject all clears the plan. Escape closes without writing.
4. Edit the target in another view, then Apply: the proposal shows Expired and the server returns 409.
5. A Mesh suggestion still creates a link on Apply and hides on Dismiss, with the shared card actions.
6. Keyboard: tab through the dialog, toggle a checkbox, activate Approve selected and Reject all.
7. `npm run lint` is clean.
